MERGE (p16:Project {name: 'Drona', description: 'Drona is a Data Science tool for utilizing Machine Learningin Exploration domain.It is a web-application that enables users to create machine learning models on well log data, tune them and deploy them to perform automatic lithofacies interpretation as well as intrapolation of gaps in well logs through curve prediction. The user is provided with a choice of Classification and Regression algorithms including in-house implemented Multivariate Bayesian Model and Scikit-learn provided algorithms such as Logistic Regression,Linear regression, K-Nearest neighbours, Artificial neural networks, Support Vector Machines and Random Forest. The software also provides visualization facility through integration of in-house developed logging software “Logger” developed by Computer Services, E&D Directorate. The process of facies identification becomes significantly faster with reduced time & effort for any target well in a Geological environment, leading to greater operational & economical efficiencies. Similarly, performing curve prediction for missing and unavailable logs, helps in providing a suitable alternative in the form of a synthetically generated data. Over a period of time when the system becomes more & more trained, it will be able to predict the missing opportunities for increased rate of success, resulting in significant cost benefits for the organization.', tagline: 'Drona is a data Science tool for leveraging Machine Learningin Exploration domain.It enables users to create machine learning models on well log data, tune them and deploy them to perform automatic lithofacies interpretation as well as filling gaps in well logs.', developed_on: '2024'});
